ScriptCast media — third-party notice

This crate adapts algorithms from HyperFrames
(https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. The license text is LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

Adapted sources:

- packages/core/src/audioCarve.ts
  Carve strength profile, third-octave speech-band centres, intelligibility
  weighting, and the Welch power-spectrum band picker.
- packages/core/src/fft.ts
  In-place radix-2 FFT used by that picker.
- skills/media-use/scripts/lib/duck.mjs
  Merging speech intervals, and the 150 ms attack / 400 ms release timing.

ScriptCast changes: speech times come from episode_manifest.json turn
windows, not from re-detecting speech in the waveform. While a window is
open the bed ducks by a fixed depth from the carve profile. HyperFrames'
measured headroom match (analyseCarveDuck) is not ported; its headroom
figure is still produced by carve_profile so the strength curve matches.

